pr_review_comments:
["```suggestion
            const nodeWithAsyncKeyword =
                (node.parent.type === "MethodDefinition" && node.parent.value === node) ||
                (node.parent.type === "Property" && node.parent.method && node.parent.value === node)
                    ? node.parent
                    : node;
```

In this case:

```js
/* eslint require-await: "error" */

const obj = {
    async: async function foo() {
        bar();
    }
}
```

suggestion would remove the wrong `await`:

```js
/* eslint require-await: "error" */

const obj = {
    : async function foo() {
        bar();
    }
}
```

It would be good to also add a test case with his example.", "```suggestion
            const asyncToken = sourceCode.getFirstToken(nodeWithAsyncKeyword, token => token.value === "async");

            return [asyncToken.range[0], sourceCode.getTokenAfter(asyncToken).range[0]]
```

We can simplify this by using tokens, and also remove extra whitespace before the next token.", "Oh, sweet! I didn't realise you could get the individual tokens. 🤦‍♂️ ", "Shouldn't we only remove `async` and leave space alone? Currently we will remove comments", "We could use just the range of the `async` keyword and extend it by one character if the next character is a space. 

I'll add a test with a comment after the `async` keyword to verify that it won't end up being removed (it currently is removed, as you point out).", "`asyncRange` is always an object. I'm not sure if `asyncToken` can ever be falsy. At least I think this should never happen in JavaScript. If we want to keep this ternary expression on `asyncToken` (not `asyncRange`), maybe it would be better to move the logic that calculates `asyncRange`, `nextToken` and `addSemiColon` into the fixer function, so that they're not calculated unnecessarily when no suggestion is provided. But I'd be also fine with assuming that `asyncToken` is always an object and dropping the check. Thoughts?", "Ah, good spotting. The ternary was left over from when the suggestion was not provided because ASI was in use. Now that we add a semicolon when ASI is in use, the ternary is no longer needed. I'll remove it.", "In this case, suggestion adds unnecessary `;`:

```js
/* eslint require-await: "error" */

class C {
    foo() {}
    async [bar] () { baz; }
}
```", "Perhaps we could add `&& prevNode.parent.parent.type !== "MethodDefinition"` here to fix this:

https://github.com/eslint/eslint/blob/48117b27e98639ffe7e78a230bfad9a93039fb7f/lib/rules/utils/ast-utils.js#L1109", "👍 Nice. That fixes it and doesn't break anything else."]

