```js
// allowVoid: false
new Promise(r => {
  // invalid
  return 1;
});

// currently this doesn't work, allowing it is just adding one more condition, let me know what you think
// allowVoid: true
new Promise(r => {
  // valid
  return void 1;
});
```
", "@mdjermanovic you [mentioned](https://github.com/eslint/eslint/pull/17282#issuecomment-1592795923) we shouldn't be doing autofix for this, but then showed an autofix example a couple comments later. I also don't believe we should be autofixing. Has your opinion changed?", "> @mdjermanovic you [mentioned](https://github.com/eslint/eslint/pull/17282#issuecomment-1592795923) we shouldn't be doing autofix for this, but then showed an autofix example a couple comments later. I also don't believe we should be autofixing. Has your opinion changed?

Well it is a confusing conversation

